283 - O Jesus, Thou Art Standing
 / 
Key: D
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 283
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[D]O Jesus, thou art standing,
[D]outside the fast [G]closed door,
[D]in lowly patience waiting
[D]to [Em/G]pass the threshold [A7]o'er:
[D]O [Bm]shame, professing [Em]Christians,
[Em]his Name [D/F#]and [E7]sign who bear,
[D]O shame, thrice shame upon us,
[D]to [Em/G]keep [G]him [A]standing there!

Verse 2:
[D]O Jesus, thou art knocking;
[D]and lo, that hand [G]is scarred,
[D]and thorns thy brow encircle,
[D]and [Em/G]tears thy face [F#m/A]have [A7]marred:
[D]O [Bm]love that passeth [Em]knowledge,
[Em]so patiently [E7]to wait!
[D]O sin that hath no equal,
[D]so [Em/G]fast [G]to [A]bar the gate!

Verse 3:
[D]O Jesus, thou art pleading
[D]in accents meek [G]and low,
[D]"I died for you, my children,
[D]and [Em/G]will you treat [F#m/A]me [A7]so?"
[D]O [Bm]Lord, with shame and [Em]sorrow
[Em]we open [E7]now the door;
[D]dear Savior, enter, enter,
[D]and [Em/G]leave [G]us [A]never more.
